    <item>
      <title>CQD-SHAP published by Springer</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/post/cqd-shap-published/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/post/cqd-shap-published/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Our paper, &lt;a href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/publication/cqd-shap/&#34;&gt;&lt;em&gt;CQD-SHAP: Explainable Complex Query Answering via Shapley Values&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, is now officially published in &lt;em&gt;Machine Learning and Knowledge Discovery in Databases&lt;/em&gt; (ECML PKDD 2026), Lecture Notes in Computer Science, by Springer. Read it on &lt;a href=&#34;https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-032-37673-2_19&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Springer&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>CQD-SHAP preprint updated on arXiv</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/post/cqd-shap-arxiv-update/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 22 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/post/cqd-shap-arxiv-update/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;We updated our preprint &lt;a href=&#34;https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.15623&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;&lt;em&gt;CQD-SHAP: Explainable Complex Query Answering via Shapley Values&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; on &lt;a href=&#34;https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.15623&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;arXiv&lt;/a&gt;. The updated codebase to reproduce our experiments is also available on &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/ds-jrg/CQD-SHAP&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;GitHub&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>CQD-SHAP accepted at ECML PKDD 2026</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/post/cqd-shap-accepted/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 28 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/post/cqd-shap-accepted/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Our paper, &lt;a href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/publication/cqd-shap/&#34;&gt;&lt;em&gt;CQD-SHAP: Explainable Complex Query Answering via Shapley Values&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, has been accepted at &lt;a href=&#34;https://ecmlpkdd.org/2026/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;ECML PKDD 2026&lt;/a&gt; in Naples, Italy. Joint work with &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.uni-paderborn.de/person/11871&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Dr. Stefan Heindorf&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I will present the work on September 9 at 12:05 in the session &lt;em&gt;&amp;ldquo;Structured Graphs, Causal &amp;amp; Relational Learning.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/em&gt; The poster session will take place the same day, from 7 to 9 PM.&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
